OL,3,GNEWSABeach oil clean-up will take
OL,4,A'several days'
OL,5,
OL,6,FBeaches in part of Kent remain closed
OL,7,Fas a major clean-up operation continues
OL,8,Ffollowing the discovery of oil deposits
OL,9,Falong the coastline.
OL,11,FThanet District Council said a
OL,12,F"significant" amount of oil was found
OL,13,Fon 18 beaches on Wednesday, prompting
OL,14,Fwidespread closures.
OL,16,FClean-up crews began work on Thursday,
OL,17,Fwith residents, especially dog owners,
OL,18,Fbeing urged to avoid the affected
OL,19,Fareas.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,323,320,200,140,0,100
